       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine's labeled maximum is 10 mg once daily, so 50 mg is five times the maximum. At that dose there is a serious risk of profound hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Amlodipine's long half-life (30 to 50 hours) would make the effects last.\n\nIs 50 mg a typo for 5 mg? If so, I can enter 5 mg by mouth once daily, which is a standard starting dose. The usual range is 2.5 to 10 mg once daily. Or, if you want a different dose within that range, tell me what it is.\n\nIf you meant to give a higher total antihypertensive effect, the usual next step is to add a second agent, such as an ACE inhibitor, an ARB, or a thiazide-like diuretic. I can enter that order if you give me the details."
